# Peer backtesting libraries for the bench.yml cross-library benchmark, plus
# maturin to build the wheel the benchmark measures. Loose source spec; the
# pinned, hash-locked output is generated from this:
#   bench.txt  (Python 3.11)  via scripts/update-lockfiles.sh
# bench.yml runs on a single Python version, so one output suffices.
maturin
backtrader
vectorbt
# vectorbt 1.1.0 imports plotly's `scattermapbox`, which plotly renamed in 6.0,
# so a fresh resolve without this pin produces a lock whose vectorbt cannot be
# imported at all -- and the benchmark would silently skip it, since a peer that
# fails to import is treated as "not installed".
plotly<6
